# M1 / B013 — configuration, custom-settings, dependency-injection, development-workflow.

C R177 OL GOV-021 | MUST | When an approved CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md value is added, changed or removed, record it under a stable setting name and identify and update every affected surface (old value and setting name, validators and DTO constraints, Domain/Application checks, database mapping, frontend validation and UI hints, tests and test data, documentation and examples, mirrored configuration), updating only affected behavior; search for stale references, build, test and run verify; one changed literal does not establish synchronization. | CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md changes | none stated
C R178 OL PST-009 | MUST | When a setting affects schema constraints, indexes, column lengths or other persistence metadata, run the persistence-change workflow (Schema-Affecting Settings). | schema-affecting settings | none stated
C R179 OL GOV-002 | MUST | Before planning or implementing a new application or substantial feature, read SPECIFICATION.md and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md. | new applications and substantial features | none stated
C R180 OL WF-001 | MUST | Inspect the relevant existing code before a non-trivial change and apply the governing rules and skills; for greenfield work or unopened files read the owning rules explicitly before writing code. | non-trivial changes | none stated
C R181 OL GOV-018 | MUST | Raise material concerns about a questionable request before implementing it. | requests | none stated
C R182 OL RUN-012 | MUST | A performance-motivated change identifies the actual bottleneck or cost, preserves observable behavior, prefers the simplest optimization that addresses it, adds or preserves tests for the affected behavior and benchmarks or profiles non-obvious or complex optimizations. | performance changes | none stated
C R183 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run the code-review workflow (or the read-only code-reviewer agent) before final verification and fix the findings that matter. | substantial work | none stated
C R184 OL WF-003 | MUST | Run the verify workflow before declaring work complete. | all implementation work | none stated

